#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059731 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059544 :question/id #uuid "dfc10727-c0d7-5b83-a4f6-afe3eb4831cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4324" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}$. Given that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$, find the value of $t$." :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$ ($\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are perpendicular) if and only if $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot t \\\\  & =-8-10+t \\\\  & =t-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ t-18 & =0 \\\\ t & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8bff08bf-0035-5f05-9607-493b301e8717" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048187 :topic/math-academy-id 430 :topic/title "Solving Equations Using the Square Root Method"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050938 :topic/math-academy-id 243 :topic/title "Calculating the Dot Product Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae77e54a-32d3-50f9-90e1-d721c6912eb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057565} {:answer/id #uuid "bef01f32-2af6-504c-9185-33a340c040ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057566} {:answer/id #uuid "05f7dc59-7d31-5a4e-b1a7-5bcc62a410e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057567} {:answer/id #uuid "126b8159-3ed9-5704-855e-553385d3d53f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218605756