/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236152} {:answer/id #uuid "49bebe95-7d8f-5363-8791-a41d117d2f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236287} {:answer/id #uuid "77b5df1a-8495-5220-8d4a-3d2d72b7ceae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236568} {:answer/id #uuid "84346316-be9d-55ce-ad43-19e661050d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236640} {:answer/id #uuid "9da633c8-52af-507c-8a35-a65c81ee25b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77b5df1a-8495-5220-8d4a-3d2d72b7ceae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236568} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f7b6300-7056-5f11-ba41-499cc6516307" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237521}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfd0ffab-79f2-5643-9530-8f55bce579c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-101417" :question/problem "Let $u=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 2x\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $u⊥v$ and $x<0$, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $u⊥v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-2)+2x\\cdot x \\\\  & =-18+2{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ -18+2{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =18 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $x<0.$ Therefore, $x=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6896d0d5-0d79-5756-b49d-54e6544b747c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267074} {:answer/id #uuid "739434d2-a34f-51ba-85b2-ecb051fb40b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267159} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9709bd-77ac-5c62-901d-3e693169f7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267686} {:answer/id #uuid "d662411b-1715-5ff4-8a35-4927cc146fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268054} {:answer/id #uuid "d927e205-8536-566a-9f6c-22e1afa9f648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "739434d2-a34f-51ba-85b2-ecb051fb40b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267159} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6039b6c-4aa0-5bb3-9ed0-9729597efec4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268702}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "214450de-6c4e-5468-90b3-b289da0c12f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-1348" :question/problem "Let $p=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ n\\end{bmatrix}$ and $q=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $p⊥q$, find the value of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $p⊥q$ ($p$ and $q$ are perpendicular) if and only if $p\\cdot q=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 4+n\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =28-4n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 28-4n & =0 \\\\ 28 & =4n \\\\ n & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cdf7785-cbcd-5112-bc95-0ebbc936c864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285506} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3e8d51-22f5-56d9-bed9-0046f6689fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285779} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2594eb-bee1-5bc9-9567-d9bdbbe0c102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286647} {:answer/id #uuid "cd97d40d-cba1-5ada-8396-a11d2d4f6bbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286658} {:answer/id #uuid "e137dd90-b672-5a36-ac92-f22334af1df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd97d40d-cba1-5ada-8396-a11d2d4f6bbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286658} :answer-field/id #uuid "126e0055-240c-57c8-bdd7-5831adf2287c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287177}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9064a6be-d660-5dcb-af2d-9691a386096a" :question/math-academy-id "q-19023" :question/problem "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}{r}^{2} \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ {r}^{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot {r}^{2}+(-6)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}-{r}^{2}-12 \\\\  & =2{r}^{2}-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =6 \\\\ r & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\sqrt{6}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "050de492-c23d-5e5a-9515-f5292836bf29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "050de492-c23d-5e5a-9515-f5292836bf29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297577} :answer-field/id #uuid "af74f5ad-0374-5f9e-bd30-ae2ff4e64785" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299231}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6840a760-5144-5da8-bd56-8faedecfd9c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-317932" :question/problem "If $c=\\begin{bmatrix}k \\\\ 2k \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},$ $d=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},$ and $c⊥d,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $c⊥d$ ($c$ and $d$ are perpendicular) if and only if $c\\cdot d=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & ={c}_{x}\\cdot {d}_{x}+{c}_{y}\\cdot {d}_{y}+{c}_{z}\\cdot {d}_{z} \\\\  & =k\\cdot (-3)+2k\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3k+4k+8 \\\\  & =k+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & =0 \\\\ k+8 & =0 \\\\ k & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc42bda9-d3c0-5507-b933-0b2f39398215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc42bda9-d3c0-5507-b933-0b2f39398215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298373} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0941247-a978-51c6-9a76-00d8d070c636" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299169}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d22ee02b-54e6-511a-8cc5-59280c888981" :question/math-academy-id "q-317945" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2{x}^{2},-4⟩$ and $b=⟨8,4⟩.$ If $a⊥b$ and $x>0,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $a⊥b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}\\cdot 8+(-4)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16{x}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ 16{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $x>0.$ Therefore, $x=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345278 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb6caf7-964e-584f-8548-449063ff8736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342474} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6655fa-a76a-596f-a2ad-fcfeda7271b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343014} {:answer/id #uuid "683aa6b1-adb6-5752-98f4-3a273931868b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343127} {:answer/id #uuid "78d230ed-b93e-5bce-ae61-1e6e00da2e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343280} {:answer/id #uuid "d7db328f-e4c7-567e-b319-dbb4a9fef103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7db328f-e4c7-567e-b319-dbb4a9fef103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344135} :answer-field/id #uuid "67145e24-54e9-57c2-bd15-3f132d50bd30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344667}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b9597aa-ca6f-577e-9d42-415936c8f19c" :question/math-academy-id "q-77152" :question/problem "Let $u=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $u⊥v$ and $a<0$, find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $u⊥v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y}+{u}_{z}\\cdot {v}_{z} \\\\  & =a\\cdot a+2\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={a}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =16 \\\\ a & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $a<0.$ Therefore, $a=-4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497648 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30d15905-64e8-5d18-af76-8acc9e5d07c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497652} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad8e45f-0ef5-5613-af41-2fd293933b76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497659} {:answer/id #uuid "53d58eb0-0d8f-5cbb-9b43-03bddd83341c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497660} {:answer/id #uuid "5d488039-835c-51f7-98f3-a614ceeaa760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497663} {:answer/id #uuid "5e52e799-9a4a-574e-8348-452560e7951d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53d58eb0-0d8f-5cbb-9b43-03bddd83341c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497660} :answer-field/id #uuid "34df9243-805f-538d-a45b-1fa7022afbc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497655}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0dfb24ed-71db-576c-87d7-7b45fd0ad875" :question/problem "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ {r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r>0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot {r}^{2}+(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-2{r}^{2}-6 \\\\  & =2{r}^{2}-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =3 \\\\ r & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $r>0.$ Therefore, $r=\\sqrt{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02e71aa6-0dd2-528b-82f1-c11f714a943c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497645} {:answer/id #uuid "31546151-ec15-571b-a3a0-a043f97c6ce6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497653} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9d1a62-29c0-5978-a42e-05d68ed3f2c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497674} {:answer/id #uuid "b6def8f7-fa98-5672-a10e-3350a588cd82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497682} {:answer/id #uuid "cf664727-ae67-5808-8037-46c3d58535a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9d1a62-29c0-5978-a42e-05d68ed3f2c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497674} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7fa0ba8-9797-51f1-a1a3-612a76531ff7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497691}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38cba23b-122c-5771-b6e6-8755391889ee" :question/problem "Let $u=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $u⊥v$ and $a<0$, find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $u⊥v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y}+{u}_{z}\\cdot {v}_{z} \\\\  & =a\\cdot a+2\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={a}^{2}-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =10 \\\\ a & =\\pm \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $a<0.$ Therefore, $a=-\\sqrt{10}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497669 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4110b4e-1a2c-578a-8eae-e4ee8ea9f987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4110b4e-1a2c-578a-8eae-e4ee8ea9f987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497681} :answer-field/id #uuid "580d3caf-8d8c-5d43-990c-bd6328480355" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497662}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "773eaa1c-93aa-5388-970f-8375245372c9" :question/problem "If $c=\\begin{bmatrix}k \\\\ 3k \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},$ $d=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},$ and $c⊥d,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $c⊥d$ ($c$ and $d$ are perpendicular) if and only if $c\\cdot d=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & ={c}_{x}\\cdot {d}_{x}+{c}_{y}\\cdot {d}_{y}+{c}_{z}\\cdot {d}_{z} \\\\  & =k\\cdot (-3)+3k\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3k+6k-8 \\\\  & =3k-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & =0 \\\\ 3k-8 & =0 \\\\ k & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07b3972e-c239-511d-a71c-02f341be9035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497646} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd291ac-ba38-5d8a-a0e8-3f5f1fe8366e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497650} {:answer/id #uuid "2c7913a5-a7e3-5bdd-8171-688ecb016f91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497651} {:answer/id #uuid "99847163-4548-58d7-8f0d-3fe134152ee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497677} {:answer/id #uuid "f30e7da8-4149-5bae-bf57-17a518398e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99847163-4548-58d7-8f0d-3fe134152ee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497677} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dd99b61-9868-53dd-b83f-1601d4f65c22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497647}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7db3af69-69b0-5a51-a3ca-bf5d1a73cdb2" :question/problem "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}4{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-10)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8{r}^{2}-4{r}^{2}-30 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2}-30 & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2} & =30 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497673 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63819dbc-3f41-5891-90a4-cfb3d79f6d2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497665} {:answer/id #uuid "64b8a2f4-8a4c-594f-b127-67b2ef09e03a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{24}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497666} {:answer/id #uuid "9db5fe94-6940-5997-81bf-5f9c1b0e4a07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497680} {:answer/id #uuid "db36b01b-c74b-5c77-9f0e-c9e4710cea66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497689} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d6ae85-eb27-5a4a-b111-5532e22cf397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db36b01b-c74b-5c77-9f0e-c9e4710cea66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497689} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba1b053-f29b-56e3-92de-9c65917d5a48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497670}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "85909f08-7094-52c8-bf85-b4e47bc2b8a0" :question/problem "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}3{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-8)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9{r}^{2}-4{r}^{2}-24 \\\\  & =5{r}^{2}-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 5{r}^{2}-24 & =0 \\\\ 5{r}^{2} & =24 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{24}{5} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b27be4c-f581-5458-a959-2633136524b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b27be4c-f581-5458-a959-2633136524b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497678} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ff7f755-1ffc-5fd4-8059-46a3459e8c06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497672}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d00137d5-07f7-5c87-9146-2b0f0101752e" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨{x}^{2},-1⟩$ and $b=⟨2,2⟩.$ If $a⊥b$ and $x<0,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $a⊥b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $x<0.$ Therefore, $x=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497690 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d1acb72-e017-5d70-8eb9-4fdfdb674352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d1acb72-e017-5d70-8eb9-4fdfdb674352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497679} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ca76dfd-af74-5089-be0d-ba18af8c7da4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497675}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e46cbde8-81fd-5138-9b25-b9d9d745ebf8" :question/problem "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}4{r}^{2} \\\\ -4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3{r}^{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$\n\n$r=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 3{r}^{2}+(-9)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =16{r}^{2}-12{r}^{2}-18 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2} & =18 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497694 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42db0ff9-268e-5f06-9ee9-a7a292ada277" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497658} {:answer/id #uuid "541c0827-2258-5054-8eab-97190e4c34ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497661} {:answer/id #uuid "6e1e2d11-8aba-58cf-8e55-5dc3a26baf88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497667} {:answer/id #uuid "9772a7d0-6381-5b37-bd93-ae02579c6810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497676} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0f7956-57e7-5c50-a0a6-2bb730385d88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e1e2d11-8aba-58cf-8e55-5dc3a26baf88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497667} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d772c8-782b-58a2-9298-f17510ff6220" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497688}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f59e3fe2-2803-5ba9-843a-699370832a34" :question/problem "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}3{r}^{2} \\\\ -4 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r>0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-6)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12{r}^{2}-8{r}^{2}-18 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2} & =18 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $r>0.$ Therefore, $r=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338258b5-5456-514c-8754-93cf8061091f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497654} {:answer/id #uuid "38237f4f-5129-5256-b140-edb70815c42b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497656} {:answer/id #uuid "714a3214-aa60-50f0-aade-4841169775f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497668} {:answer/id #uuid "c06c6172-5411-5aa2-9336-178c2ad14341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497684} {:answer/id #uuid "cec53d7c-f38a-5d49-be8a-32db3b6b3e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "714a3214-aa60-50f0-aade-4841169775f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497668} :answer-field/id #uuid "14f6fb08-46af-5637-b16c-c9f11df73b8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497649}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff91a7cd-801d-551f-898a-f82e597274c3" :question/problem "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}4{r}^{2} \\\\ -3 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r>0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-10)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12{r}^{2}-6{r}^{2}-20 \\\\  & =6{r}^{2}-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 6{r}^{2}-20 & =0 \\\\ 6{r}^{2} & =20 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{10}{3} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $r>0.$ Therefore, $r=\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{3}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given Two Perpendicular Vectors"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100817 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100609 :question/id #uuid "1579f932-6e7f-5daa-b001-54a9f6c236ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-14406" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2 }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3({log}_{3}⁡x)^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097bf9be-35d0-5117-aeeb-185f65a4e444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295316} {:answer/id #uuid "0c595f3e-4a64-5335-bfee-ef4f9c199d44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295335} {:answer/id #uuid "3a9d8072-eeac-5190-ac53-423bbc5c0d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295602} {:answer/id #uuid "7c854fd3-91d0-5ade-bfec-4aa656855a88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295948} {:answer/id #uuid "943f1ef0-98c7-561c-8c98-1ab90aa0f4c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "943f1ef0-98c7-561c-8c98-1ab90aa0f4c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296059} :answer-field/id #uuid "94521d82-e55e-520c-aa39-65e9dae6d07e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296944}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc1950d7-cc9c-5e9a-8f86-5dcc05de2e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-31329" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27327c99-efb7-58e8-a74e-787cf861a36a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{log}_{2}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295482} {:answer/id #uuid "87c24d2f-2c74-5040-90ac-f36195ad44b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295999} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd76f53-ed5e-50ea-9b0a-4825cbde5b04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x{log}_{3}^{2}⁡x}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296097} {:answer/id #uuid "cee39ee1-4f54-5380-b841-9cb4997a9fd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}){log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296353} {:answer/id #uuid "e80a0ef7-8043-5002-b2dc-df0cdf73346a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87c24d2f-2c74-5040-90ac-f36195ad44b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295999} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e8e1d5-6ca1-583b-a916-cb7fac5a8d3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296934}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8e9ea16-ddaf-5f82-ac82-079325b04f6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-31401" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}).$Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\int u\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101536 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "383be394-a41f-5e0f-b93b-a0ff9878be08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{7}⁡(4x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339635} {:answer/id #uuid "750a3dcf-e361-507f-ad62-9dbb75727d78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{7}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340176} {:answer/id #uuid "aa31712a-2e4f-527b-a00c-e331135a4450" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{7}⁡(4x)|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340682} {:answer/id #uuid "dc05d22a-2a20-518f-afa3-1ccc9267a967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{7}⁡({x}^{4})|+C" :db/id #e