on/id #uuid "d5cc7305-f37c-53f7-a090-f87a05c29da3" :question/math-academy-id "q-73654" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{x{log}_{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{x{log}_{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{log}_{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =4{ln}^{2}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d6f093e-f768-5e62-ade0-cf5596e4cd1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267107} {:answer/id #uuid "86209d84-5f42-5574-8ad3-0e47879b9965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267327} {:answer/id #uuid "870b3329-aa01-5f17-9195-ecc19a4828b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267336} {:answer/id #uuid "9e67db5a-0313-599c-9c9f-de8434f5f20e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267571} {:answer/id #uuid "b99c433b-c983-52f0-b3d5-5926af31a475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "870b3329-aa01-5f17-9195-ecc19a4828b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267336} :answer-field/id #uuid "55ad0e89-e68a-51f1-9876-435c573c4ae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268561}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ee2e00a-8c3c-5799-9d71-e6ddab6853db" :question/math-academy-id "q-13837" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | ${e}^{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={\\frac{{u}^{2}}{3}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f8e4b7e-6484-54d8-82ef-905057fbfe3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266274} {:answer/id #uuid "171b3ebd-28f1-5159-9586-ca3b0ad1e1c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266333} {:answer/id #uuid "c46c5362-21f4-5da6-a3af-f4cf5a5e87ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267899} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb69016-0981-5564-a216-f5aa929c2431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267993} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a9f8db-caf5-5753-9bbd-1d64a0f8ff58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c46c5362-21f4-5da6-a3af-f4cf5a5e87ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267899} :answer-field/id #uuid "5563d6e5-dc15-5788-932c-de927f8d699c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268560}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "71f1a3c4-8374-541a-b0a7-9306ac0ecfa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-13841" :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e/2}^{{e}^{2}/2}\\frac{2}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2x}\\cdot 2=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e/2$ | ${e}^{2}/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e/2}^{{e}^{2}/2}\\frac{2}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{e/2}^{{e}^{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "849b6357-4405-5be3-92d3-690a94a05de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}((\\operatorname{ln}⁡4